course: dictionary
lesson: 4646
title: Historic: important, or old and worth keeping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Historic has two meanings. The first is important in history, or likely to be remembered later as important. «The astronauts made a historic moment when they landed on the Moon.» The landing changed what people knew, so people will remember it.
explain: The second meaning is about old places and things from the past that are worth keeping. «We visited a historic castle with thick stone walls.» The word castle is a clue: it is an old building that is kept safe. A «historic town centre» is an old part of a town.
explain: Context helps you choose. In sport, «a historic win» is a very special first, so the win will be remembered. Ask yourself: is this about something important that happened, or about something old that is worth keeping?
explain: Grammar uses the word in a special name too. «The historic present tells a past story in the present tense to make it exciting; in written stories you usually choose one tense and keep it.» Here historic is part of a grammar term, so the context tells you it is not about the old buildings.
fact: Historic means important in history, or likely to be remembered in the future as important.
fact: Historic also describes old buildings, places or things from the past that are worth keeping.
fact: Famous historic moments include the Moon landing in 1969 and the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989.
fact: Useful phrases include historic moment, historic building, historic site and historic day.
fact: Historic is related to history, which is the study of the past.
exercise: «The historic moment was shown on TV all over the world.» What does historic mean here? | Quiet and small | Very cold and wet | Old and falling down | * Important, and remembered for a long time
exercise: «They walked around the historic town centre, looking at the old stone houses.» What does historic describe? | A new shopping mall | A busy sports game | * An old part of a town worth keeping | A loud market day
exercise: Her team's «historic win» was the first in fifty years. What makes the win historic? | * It was a very special first | It was played by very old players | It was played in the rain | It ended in a draw
test: «The Berlin Wall fell in 1989, a historic day for many people.» What does historic mean? | * Important in history | Cold and grey | Very old and broken | Funny
test: Which phrase describes an old building worth keeping? | A historic win | * A historic building | A historic joke | A historic goal
exam: Which sentence shows historic meaning important in history? | We ate lunch by the old harbour | * The peace treaty was signed on a historic day | The puppy was historic and fluffy | The bus was late again
